    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and both its tests pass with the full build green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the registration-date rule for `POST /api/owners`: when no registration date is supplied, it defaults to the server's current date, and `registrationDate` is returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format (LocalDate serializes that way natively).\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `LocalDate registrationDate` field mapped to a new `registration_date` column, with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Since `Owner` composes `OwnerFields` via `allOf`, this flows into both the generated request DTO (`OwnerFieldsDto`) and response DTO (`OwnerDto`), and MapStruct auto-maps it by name in both directions \u2014 no mapper changes needed.\n\n3. **`rest/function/owner/BuildOwner.java`** \u2014 after mapping the request to an `Owner`, defaults `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when the request omitted it. A supplied date passes straight through, so the \"keep supplied date\" case works too.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres` `schema.sql`) \u2014 added the `registration_date DATE` column so JPA persists and reads the field. The test profile uses `hsqldb`.\n\nThe update path (`ApplyOwner`) was left untouched, so it preserves an existing owner's registration date rather than clearing it.\n\nTest results: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 both `coreDefaultsToToday` and `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate` pass, `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
